config BR2_PACKAGE_TDVP_VGLITE_ACCEPTANCE
	bool "tdvp-vglite-acceptance"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBDRM
	select BR2_PACKAGE_VG_LITE
	help
	  Install the bounded TDVP VGLite acceptance probe.

	  The probe is deliberately not a display diagnostic: it creates an
	  off-screen DRM dumb buffer, exports it as DMA-BUF, and renders into it
	  through VGLite. It never obtains DRM master, creates a framebuffer,
	  changes a mode, commits an atomic state, or flips a page. Run it as the
	  graphical login user before enabling VGLite inside wlroots. The package
	  also installs tdvp-vglite-client-churn: a bounded, opt-in wrapper which
	  repeatedly starts and exits this same off-screen probe while a VGLite
	  Labwc session is already active, testing the per-file kernel resource
	  ownership boundary without altering KMS state. The companion
	  tdvp-vglite-session-gate verifies the actual Labwc process environment
	  and renderer policy before running the fixed-panel wl_shm benchmark and
	  that churn workload; it never enables VGLite or changes the session.
	  tdvp-vglite-inflight-close-gate is a separate, opt-in fault-injection
	  command: it submits one off-screen command, exits without WAIT, then
	  proves that a new VGLite client can run normally after kernel recovery.

comment "tdvp-vglite-acceptance needs a toolchain w/ threads"
	depends on !BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
